+/// `struct input_event` opens with a `timeval`, which is two C longs wide, so
+/// the struct is 24 bytes on a 64-bit kernel and **16 on a 32-bit one** such as
+/// the Miyoo Mini Flip's armv7. Reading 24-byte records out of a 16-byte stream
+/// slides every field: the timestamp lands where type/code/value are read from,
+/// so every press decodes as garbage and is dropped. Derive it instead of
+/// assuming the aarch64 layout.
+const TIME_BYTES: usize = 2 * std::mem::size_of::<libc::c_long>();
+
+pub const EVENT_BYTES: usize = TIME_BYTES + 8;
 
